script = ExtResource("1_c82dc")
dialogue_id = "debate_magic_self_harm"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Magic Rituals"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Back when the priests among our ancestors practiced magical rituals, they settled a shard we now call The Fox Spirits Domain.
historian: When they first met these foxes, they considered them evil spirits, and tried to ward them off by performing blood sacrifice.
historian: Their descendants on that shard took this lesson to heart.
historian: Now, they bleed themselves to cure a fever and to beg the heavens for rain.
historian: It is a strange thing, how easily we can convince ourselves that suffering is a holy act.
historian: When we decide that a painful ritual is what the heavens demand, we stop looking for practical solutions.
historian: We are often told that the hardships of trying to rebuild the Old World are a necessary, holy sacrifice.
historian: But pain is not a currency that buys us favor with the universe.
historian: It is just pain.
historian: We should choose a path that seeks to heal our communities, rather than proving our devotion by how much we are willing to hurt ourselves."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
